Wildvine possesses chlorokinesis, the ability to telepathically interface with plant life. This was first demonstrated by [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] in his [[Weapon XI (Flashback)|second amalgamation form]], where he used this ability to trap the Tennysons and his own teammates within thick vines.<ref>''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref> Another demonstration of this ability was seen by [[Albedo|Negative]] Wildvine, who was able to remotely ensnare multiple individuals onto tables with vines.<ref name="The Ultimate Heist">''[[The Ultimate Heist]]''</ref>

Wildvine has minor shapeshifting abilities, being able to transform his arms into whip-like tendrils that he can use against opponents.<ref name="RT">''[[Rook Tales]]''</ref> He can also enlarge his flytrap to a size that can fit an entire person.<ref name="SOTO" /> Furthermore, Wildvine has control over his cellular growth, which allows him to extend his limbs and arms{{Refn|[[:File:Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures Pop-up (19).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="SAHBA">''[[Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures (Episode)|Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures]]''</ref> to suit his movement needs.{{Refn|[[:File:Wildvine Movement Duncan.png]]|group = DR}}{{Refn|[[:File:Wildvine Movement Dave Johnson.png]]|group = DJ}} Using this power, Wildvine turns his limbs into prehensile vine-like tendrils to grab and restrain others.<ref name="BW">''[[Benwolf]]''</ref> Additionally, using his elastic limbs, Wildvine can swing around at great speeds,<ref name="SAHBA" /> and grab bars and poles.<ref name="MM" />

Wildvine can grow black fruits{{Refn|https://archive.is/IULEs|name = DJ|group = DJ}} (also referred to as spore pods){{Refn|[[:File:Wildvine 00.png|Wildvine 00.png]]|group = CN}} on his back that contain a whole host of substances, allowing him to use them as explosives<ref name="RT" /> or gas bombs.<ref name="MM" /> His fruits can also grow vines.<ref name="RMP">''[[Rad Monster Party]]''</ref> Wildvine also can tame [[Gracklflint|Gracklflints]] using his fruits, as demonstrated by [[Pax]].<ref name="Rad" />

Wildvine can grow sharp thorns on his body.<ref name="Camp Fear">''[[Camp Fear]]''</ref><ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref> Additionally, he can also quickly tunnel underground.<ref name="RMP" />

Wildvine is able to regenerate his body if damaged, as demonstrated by Pax.<ref name="Rad">''[[Rad]]''</ref>

Wildvine possesses enhanced strength, as he was able to trap a [[Loboan (Classic)|Loboan]] in his tendrils,<ref name="BW" /> stop a falling cargo lift from landing on [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] and [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and hold it for a short time,<ref name="EE"/> and easily break rocks with his bare fists.<ref name="RMP" />

Wildvine possesses enhanced durability, as demonstrated when [[Kuphulu]] smashed him onto a building.<ref name="RMP" /> Wildvine also possesses enhanced jumping and reflexes, as shown when [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen]] as Wildvine was able to swiftly dodge a blast of electricity shot out by [[Frankenstrike]].<ref name="ATTWB" />

Wildvine doesn't breathe through any lungs, making him immune to multiple kinds of gas, such as the gas created by his fruits, and flame retardants.{{Refn|[[:File:Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures Pop-up (21).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="SAHBA" /><ref name="EE" />

Wildvine can close his flytrap, as seen during his fight with the [[Werewolf]] when he dragged him underground.<ref name="BW" /> He can also trap people by closing his flytrap, as demonstrated by the [[Florauna (Classic)|Florauna]] on [[Xenon]].<ref name="SOTO" />

Wildvine is capable of making whips by extruding tendrils out of the palms of his hands.<ref name="LDtTWA">''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref>

Wildvine can fuse himself to terrestrial plants, such as [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] trees.<ref>''[[The Visitor]]''</ref>

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====[[Savage Pursuit]]====
Wildvine is able to launch sharp plants from his body.

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
RMP (146).png|Tangled Vines
EvEnc (261).png|Elasticity Limit
</gallery>
Wildvine's vines can be tangled.<ref name="RMP" />

If Wildvine stretches himself too much, his arms will stay stretched and unable to shorten for a while.<ref name="EE" />

Wildvine has a weakness against electricity, such as that generated by an [[Amperi (Classic)|Amperi]], as demonstrated with Pax.<ref>''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]''</ref><ref name="Rad" />

Being a plant-based alien, Wildvine is particularly sensitive to extremely cold temperatures. Unless he is given his energy source, he will quickly dry up, wilt, and perish.{{Refn|[[:File:Wildvine Bandai Lenticular Card.png]]|group = Bandai}}

==History==
===Prior to Ben 10===
*[[Myaxx]] added Wildvine's DNA to the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]], unaware that the [[Florauna (Classic)|Florauna]] donor was possessed by [[Zs'Skayr]].{{Refn|[[:File:Zs'Skayr Possessed the Florauna Sample.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref>''[[Be Afraid of the Dark]]''</ref>

===Ben 10===
*Wildvine first appeared in ''[[Camp Fear]]'', where he was accidentally unlocked by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] and battled the [[Mycelium]] until he reverted.
*In ''[[Tough Luck]]'', Wildvine saved [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] and [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] from falling and defeated [[Hex (Classic)|Hex]] and [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]].
*In ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'', Wildvine appeared thrice. Firstly, he was used by the Master Control. Later, Wildvine appeared in a photo with Max and Gwen. Finally, in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]], Wildvine defeated a trio of [[Null Guardian|Null Guardians]] before switching into [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]].
*In '' [[Midnight Madness]]'', Wildvine defeated [[Sublimino]].
*In ''[[Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures (Episode)|Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures]]'', Wildvine followed [[Kane North]] to his hideout, defeated an animatronic dragon, saved [[Tim Dean]], and fought the former until he reverted.
*In ''[[Benwolf]]'', Wildvine saved Max and [[Dr. Wes Green|Wes]] from falling to their deaths and battled the [[Werewolf]] until he reverted.
*In ''[[Under Wraps]]'', Wildvine fed some pigs with Gwen.
*In ''[[The Visitor]]'', Wildvine spied on [[Xylene]] and Max.

===Five Years Prior to Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', Wildvine was used by 16-year-old Ben in 11-year-old Ben's body to battle [[Eon]] alongside 11-year-old Ben as 16-year-old [[Arctiguana]].
* In ''[[Evil's Encore]]'', Wildvine was used to help get through the [[Mt. Rushmore (Classic)|Plumber base]] that was being controlled by [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]].

===Alien Force=== 
*Wildvine was locked by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.

===Ultimate Alien=== 
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Wildvine was re-unlocked by [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Outbreak]]'', Wildvine battled [[Rook Blonko|Rook]] in a training session before switching into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', [[Albedo|​Negative]] Wildvine trapped Rook, [[Argit]], [[Fistina]], and [[Solid Plugg]] in his vines. Later, Negative Wildvine defeated [[Thirteen]].
*In ''[[Rad Monster Party]]'', Wildvine defeated [[Kuphulu]].
*In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen 10]] as Wildvine protected [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] from Negative [[Ultimate Spidermonkey]].
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Gwen 10 as Wildvine fought [[Benzarro]] as [[Frankenstrike]].
*In ''[[Rook Tales]]'', Wildvine was defeated by [[Kundo]].
*In ''[[Breakpoint]]'', Wildvine was used to go undercover in [[Fistrick|Fistrick's]] gang thrice.
*In ''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]'', [[Skurd]] gave [[Feedback]] Wildvine's tendrils to battle [[Subdora]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Wildvine appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]=== 
*In ''[[Ken 10]]'', [[Ken Tennyson|Ken]] as Wildvine beat [[Devlin Levin|Devlin]] at hoverboard tricks.

===Goodbye and Good Riddance (What-If?)===
*In ''[[Goodbye and Good Riddance]]'', Wildvine battled some criminals who hijacked a blimp.

