==Trivia== 
*Wildvine's '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' color scheme is similar to those of the [[Florauna (Classic)|Florauna]] tribe found on [[Xenon]] from '''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix|Secret of the Omnitrix]]'''''.
*The [[Omnitrix (Gweniverse)|Omnitrix]] symbol on [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen 10]]'s version of Wildvine is circular like her male counterparts, instead of having a cat-like shape like Gwen's other aliens.
*Wildvine and [[Ditto]] are the only aliens to be manually (and accidentally) unlocked by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].
*Wildvine is the first alien [[Albedo]] turned into on-screen with the [[Ultimatrix (Stabilizer)|recreated Ultimatrix]].
*[[Dave Johnson]] designed Wildvine and came up with the idea that he could rip off the fruits from his back and throw it like grenades, which [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]] later tweaked.{{Refn|name = DJ|group = DJ}} His earliest rendition was called [[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)/Early Development#PlantGuy|PlantGuy]] and drawn by [[Steven E. Gordon]].
*[[Chap Yaep]] designed Gwen 10's Wildvine.{{Refn|[[:File:Chap Yaep Designed Gwen 10's Wildvine.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*The bulb-like hair of Gwen 10's Wildvine is similar to the hair of [[Wikipedia:Princess Leia|Princess Leia]] from the '''[[Wikipedia:Star Wars|Star Wars]]''' franchise.

